    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256-a33">

                <pb facs="0721" n="507" xml:id="pg507"/>

                <head>XXXIII.—Protocol of conference between the high commissioners on the part of
                    the United States of America and the high commissioners on the part of Great
                    Britain.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 25, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The high commissioners having met, the protocol of the conference held on the
                    24th of April was read and confirmed.</p>
                <p>The high commissioners then proceeded with the consideration of the matters
                    referred to them.</p>
                <p>The conference was adjourned to the 26th of April.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. C. BANCROFT DAVIS.</signed>
                    <signed>TENTERDEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
